Alpha envy??? Only two of alpha group were there.<P>I know exactly what your saying Leat. When I first started grouping with Sleethr and Ghall I wanted them to spell out to what the heck they wanted me to do. Ghall and Sleethr also have the advantage of being in the same room together.(Just wait until they are discussing something and you're waiting for a response.)<P>And when it came to moving last night, well slow exp is better than none? Yes, but both suck. Everything on my tracking menu was green, except for some dwarfs. Wait until 51+, then you'll understand.<P>With time you'll start to learn the other classes abilities more and more. And how you can work together better with them. And after being at these stagnent levels you begin to learn when to heal Ghall the uber tank, and when to hold off. You'll start to learn Sleethr's various pets, and when to heal them. <P>And when someone says EVAC do it! Don't look around to see what it is, how many, what it looks like just hit it. Thats what I tried last night, I saw someone say evac I stood up clicked and went down before I could blink. I didn't even know what was on us until I could see it from above looking at my corpse in the LOADING PLEASE WAIT screen.<P>So to sum it up. It'll take time. Got a question? Ask. Don't understand the answer, say so. But be ready to be belittled  <IMG SRC="tongue.gif" border="0"><P>--------------------<P><B>Nefarius Draconocissor</B> - 55 Perserver/Freelance Gynocologist/Traitor to Division 13<BR><B>Meretrixx</B> - 48 Warrior<BR>Bertoxxolus
