Been thinking about re-starting a <B><I>CLASS TACTICS</I></B> guide...kind of a general, what is expected guide book.<P>I'll start it here though and if it grows to beyond just my .0002 cents and gets some better counter points and detail...then I'm move/start it in a special "Tactics" guide. This is very general in nature and doesn't cover specific situations, but it is what I expect each class to be aware of when I group with them.<P>What I expect from each class in group situations:<P>Bard: Mana, Melee, Dmg Shield, Hastes, Buffs, Healing, Crowd Control, Puller, Snarer, Slower, Resist Buffer...okay...a little of everything that is highly dependant on the group makeup and targets<P>Cleric: Healing, Stuns, HP/AC Buffer, some nukes<P>Druid: Healing, Evac, Ports, Dmg Shield, Nukes, Snare, SoW and other Buffs.<P>Enchanter: Mezz, Haste, Tash, Stuns, Slow<P>Magician: Nuke, Malo, Damage Shield, Pet, Summon stuff<P>Monk: High Melee Dmg Dealer, Poor tank, FD Pull<P>Necromancer: Pet, DMF, DoT's, Snare, Fear, DD, Heal, Mana Pump, Summon Corpse<P>Paladin: High Melee Damage Taker, Medium Melee Dmg Dealer, Heals, Stuns, LoH<P>Ranger: High Melee Damage Dealer, Low Dmg Taker, Snare, Tracker/Outdoor Puller, SoW<P>Rogue: Mega-High Dmg Dealer, Low Dmg Taker, Scout, CR Expert, Lock Pick ( Highier Lvl ), Trap Detection/Removal<P>Shadow Knight: High Melee Damage Taker, Medium Melee Dmg Dealer, Snare, FD Pull, Pet, High Taunt of SK Spells<P>Shaman: Stat Buffer, Slows, Malo, DoT's, Pet, SoW<P>Warrior: High Dmg Taker and Dealer<P>Wizard: Nukes, Stuns, AoE Snare, Evac, Ports<P><BR>What's all that mean?  Means that if a druid joins my group, they should ask: <P>1) "Who's Primary Healer and is there a Secondary Healer already?"  Social hotkeys should be in place to "/g Healing %t" to let the other healers and the target know what is going on.  Nothing is more nerve wracking for a melee person about to die then not knowing if a heal is coming in or not.<BR>2) "Evac and where?"  Even if there is an evaccer already present...an Evac should ALWAYS be loaded. Preferrably to BB.  The call for evac is highly subjective, but in general if healer is LOM and tanks low on health and some adds pop up with enchanter LOM...evac first..ask questions later.<BR>3) "Someone snaring?"  Even if someone else is snaring..SNARE should ALWAYS be loaded. Since snare has high taunt, snare should be cast after main tank has managed to secure aggro, but long before mob tries to run.  If time permits, snare all mezzed mobs.  Again, hotkey "/g SNARED %t" to let group know.  Sometimes knowing exactly when and that a mob is snared can make a huge difference in the tactics used...IOW...Fear to control mob.<BR>4) "Who is the Main Tank?" 1) who to assist and 2) Who to cast dmg shield on in no one else is doing that.<BR>5) Druids should ALWAYS reserve mana for either or sometimes both...Heals and Evac.  If you're primary evaccer...NEVER fall below evac mana levels.<P>Only picked on druids here due to you asking and well...you are a druid.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>--------------------<P>Verser - Bard of the 51st Song
</FONT>
