One thing that I think other stat buffers can agree with is that all those stat buffs take LOADS and LOADS of mana.<BR>Don't expect me to buff you, be the primary healer, malo'er and slower and still be effective at anything other than getting you dead.<P>Another thing I should point out .. when I say Evac ... I mean Evac not group port.  I've been in situations as Ghall where a non-Div-13 Dr00d was doing the Evacing and got us kinda dead when they cast the LONG gate vs the short casting Evac.<P>If you are the de-buffer (ie nullify to remove DS's or SoW ... etc) PLEASE PLEASE PLEASE do that BEFORE I wast 250+ mana on my debuffs (ie Malo and Slow) it REALLY pisses me off to drop 500 mana only to have it canceled/nullified by you  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Nullify/cancel should be your first spell cast. (if you ask me)<P>Other than than I'd agree with Verser.  Try to get a feel for what you'll be fighting so you can arrange your buffs.  As Ghall I have essentially 3 spell line ups.<P>Solo Ghall, which is what I almost ALWAYS have loaded.<P>Group Ghall, Obviously I have this set up when I'm grouped.<P>Travel Ghall, For running about Norrath trying to remain alive and undetected.<P>Another thing I'd reccomend is changing your HUD layout and changing colors of things so that you can see better.  Some people are ANAL enough to have 3 or 4 .ini files set up for each different area they are fighting in.   One for Ice, Water, Jungle and Desert or something like that.  For me I just picked colors that stuck out no matter where I was even if that means running with the transparent overlay turned on  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>2 SUPER important things.<P>1.) Know the zone your gonna fight in.<BR>2.) Know the mobs that spawn there.<P>Some places like the maze in LGuck still confuse the F**K out of me and in the rain I still get turned around sometimes .. Sense heading, /Loc and maps are your friends.<P>I guess that's my 2 cents worth.<P>--------------------<P> <